 "open": "The charged exhaust, 85-95% of the flow, is a heavy-ion source about 10^5 times the solar wind's own mass flux through the aperture. Without magnets the wind loads, slows and carries it downstream over the Moon, energising picked-up oxygen to tens of keV; the loss response credits each returning pickup ion with 1-10 sputtered molecules. The September magnets hold off exhaust ions and picked-up oxygen, whose gyroradii at the magnetopause are small against the stand-off; xenon picked up at solar-wind speed gyrates on a scale near the stand-off, and entry through the cusps and by reconnection is open. No model here follows that plasma.",
